{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":1987765,"ns":0,"title":"Abutment","extract":"An abutment is the substructure at the ends of a bridge span or dam supporting its superstructure. Single-span bridges have abutments at each end that provide vertical and lateral support for the span, as well as acting as retaining walls to resist lateral movement of the earthen fill of the bridge approach.","description":"Construction substructure","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}